WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:08.090
The dilemma is always: do you make an ending that that's tidy and pat

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:14.610
so that the risk of having it be not
realistic—because tidy, pat endings, you

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:19.949
know, they're satisfying, but it's not
whatever really happens, right? Or do

00:00:19.949 --> 00:00:27.480
you have it be a little looser, in the way that real life is, at the risk

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:34.850
of having it seem too open-ended? So I've kind of done both.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:39.930
In a few of my books, I've gone to
some lengths to architect big,

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:45.270
complicated endings that all kind of
stick the landing. And in other cases I

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:51.390
haven't done so as much. 
KEVIN KELLY: On the internet there was a joke that if they

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:56.699
had given you the task of writing the
last episodes of Game of Thrones there

00:00:56.699 --> 00:00:59.670
would be two more seasons where there'd
be bureaucratic minutiae of

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:10.260
rebuilding King's Landing.
STEPHENSON: Well, I didn't get that job. But I do, yeah I

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:21.180
do see the...In that and other television
series I sometimes see things that my

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.990
initial reaction is that I'm looking at
lazy writing, but I don't know if it's...I

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:31.500
suspect what it really is is the
showrunner saying, 'Such and such thing

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:38.360
needs to happen 35 minutes into this episode, or else.' And so

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:47.250
then everything has to be rearranged to
make that occur. And so that's, I think,

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.280
when you sometimes see a character
suddenly do something that's out of

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.420
character, which I think
accounts for a lot of the dissatisfaction

00:01:54.420 --> 00:02:01.979
that people felt when with the the last
part of that TV series, kind of rushing

00:02:01.979 --> 00:02:05.770
it to a conclusion.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.829
 

